# AccessLens-IE: Widening Participation, Access Pathways & Geographic Deprivation Analytics for Irish Higher Education (2019/2020 to 2025/2026)

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/Code_License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.11%2B-3776AB.svg)](requirements.txt)
[![DuckDB](https://img.shields.io/badge/Warehouse-DuckDB_Medallion-FFF000.svg)](src/accesslens/step1_data_layer.py)
[![NAP 2022-2028](https://img.shields.io/badge/Policy-National_Access_Plan_2022--2028-006644.svg)](docs/methodology.md)

**Author:** Sohum Vivek Dhole (MSc Business Analytics, First Class Honours; BE Electronics Engineering)

**AccessLens-IE** is an end-to-end, reproducible analytics engineering and widening participation reporting pipeline built on official **Higher Education Authority (HEA)** Student Records System (SRS) public releases (`2019/2020` to `2025/2026`, `{{raw_hea_files}}` CSV tables) and the **Pobal HP Deprivation Index 2022** at Electoral Division grain (`{{pobal_ed_count}}` Electoral Divisions covering all `{{pobal_total_pop_2022}}` Census 2022 residents across `{{n_counties}}` counties).

The project evaluates higher education access pathways, mature student participation, flexible/part-time study modes, discipline mix, and county-level socio-economic catchment profiles, benchmarking **Maynooth University (MU)** against the **IUA University Sector (`{{n_iua_universities}}` universities)** and the **All HEA-Funded Institutions (`{{n_hea_institutions}}` institutions)** benchmark under the **National Access Plan (NAP) 2022-2028** indicator framework.

Every figure in this repository is rendered directly from [`outputs/audit/audit.json`](outputs/audit/audit.json) and verified by an automated `pytest` suite covering data contracts, DuckDB metric recomputation, document traceability, mutation testing, GDPR-style small-cell suppression (`<{{small_cell_threshold}}`), and formula-driven Excel/Power BI delivery.

