## Headline Audited Findings (`2019/2020` to `2025/2026`)

1. **Sustained Enrolment Expansion Outpacing Sector Benchmarks:** Maynooth University grew from **`{{mu_enrol_2019_20}}`** total enrolments in `2019/2020` to **`{{mu_enrol_2025_26}}`** in `2025/2026` (adding **`{{mu_enrol_6yr_added}}`** students, **`+{{mu_enrol_6yr_growth}}`** over six years and **`+{{mu_enrol_yoy_growth}}`** year-on-year from **`{{mu_enrol_2024_25}}`** in `2024/2025`). This outpaced both the `{{n_iua_universities}}`-university IUA group (**`+{{iua_enrol_6yr_growth}}`**, from **`{{iua_enrol_2019_20}}`** to **`{{iua_enrol_2025_26}}`**) and the full `{{n_hea_institutions}}`-institution HEA sector (**`+{{sector_enrol_6yr_growth}}`**, from **`{{sector_enrol_2019_20}}`** to **`{{sector_enrol_2025_26}}`**).
2. **Mature and Flexible Participation Composition Shift:** While Maynooth University's absolute mature (`24+`) student headcount held steady around three thousand students (**`{{mu_mature_2019_20}}`** in `2019/2020`, **`{{mu_mature_2024_25}}`** in `2024/2025`, and **`{{mu_mature_2025_26}}`** in `2025/2026`), rapid expansion in young (`23 and under`) undergraduate Honours Degree entrants (**`+{{mu_young_6yr_growth}}`**, from **`{{mu_young_2019_20}}`** to **`{{mu_young_2025_26}}`**) shifted MU's mature student share from **`{{mu_mature_share_2019_20}}`** to **`{{mu_mature_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{mu_mature_share_6yr_pp}}`**), compared with **`{{iua_mature_share_2025_26}}`** across IUA universities and **`{{sector_mature_share_2025_26}}`** across all HEA institutions. Part-time and flexible delivery at MU represents **`{{mu_flex_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{mu_pt_2025_26}}`** students) in `2025/2026`, compared with **`{{iua_flex_share_2025_26}}`** in the university sector and **`{{sector_flex_share_2025_26}}`** across the HEA sector.
3. **Foundation, Access and Non-Honours Undergraduate Pathways vs Direct Degree Entry:** Across all HEA institutions, standalone `Foundation and Access` programme enrolments rose **`+{{sector_fa_6yr_growth}}`** over six years (from **`{{sector_fa_2019_20}}`** in `2019/2020` to **`{{sector_fa_2025_26}}`** in `2025/2026`), concentrated in institutions that code foundation certificates as standalone SRS programmes: **ATU Donegal (`{{fa_atu_donegal_2025_26}}`)**, **TU Dublin City (`{{fa_tud_city_2025_26}}`)**, **Trinity College Dublin (`{{fa_tcd_2025_26}}`)**, **University of Galway (`{{fa_uog_2025_26}}`)**, and **MTU Kerry (`{{fa_mtu_kerry_2025_26}}`)**. At Maynooth University, standalone SRS `Foundation and Access` headcount is **`{{mu_fa_2025_26}}`** (**`{{mu_fa_2019_20}}`** in `2019/2020`), while broader non-honours undergraduate pathways (`Foundation and Access`, `Undergraduate Certificate`, `Undergraduate Diploma`, `Ordinary Degree`, and `Other Undergraduate`, including part-time certificates and partnership programmes) total **`{{mu_ug_pathway_2025_26}}`** students (**`{{mu_ug_pathway_share_ug_2025_26}}`** of MU's **`{{mu_ug_2025_26}}`** undergraduates and **`{{mu_ug_pathway_share_tot_2025_26}}`** of total enrolments). Honours Degrees account for **`{{mu_hons_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{mu_hons_2025_26}}`** students, up **`+{{mu_hons_6yr_growth}}`** from **`{{mu_hons_2019_20}}`**). The public data cannot show which routes HEAR, DARE or FET entrants take.
4. **Ecological County Deprivation vs Higher Education Participation:** Across Ireland's `{{n_counties}}` counties (`{{national_county_mapped_enrol_2025_26}}` county-mapped Irish-domiciled enrolments in `2025/2026`, or **`{{national_enrol_rate_1k_2025_26}}`** per `1,000` residents), county population-weighted Pobal HP relative deprivation score (`Index22_ED_std_rel_wt`) exhibits a statistically significant positive correlation with higher education participation per `1,000` residents: **Pearson $r = {{corr_rel_2025_26_r}}$** (95% CI **`{{corr_rel_2025_26_ci_low}}` to `{{corr_rel_2025_26_ci_high}}`**, $p = {{corr_rel_2025_26_p}}$) and **Spearman $\rho = {{corr_rel_2025_26_rho}}$** (95% CI **`{{corr_rel_2025_26_rho_ci_low}}` to `{{corr_rel_2025_26_rho_ci_high}}`**, $p = {{corr_rel_2025_26_rho_p}}$), with an OLS slope of **`{{corr_rel_2025_26_slope}}`** additional enrolments per `1,000` population per Pobal index point ($R^2 = {{corr_rel_2025_26_r2}}$). In the exact Census match year (`2022/2023`), Pearson $r = {{corr_rel_2022_23_r}}$ (95% CI **`{{corr_rel_2022_23_ci_low}}` to `{{corr_rel_2022_23_ci_high}}`**, $p = {{corr_rel_2022_23_p}}$).
5. **Maynooth University's Midlands, Border and South-East Catchment Reach:** While **`{{mu_core3_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{mu_core3_enrol_2025_26}}`** of MU's **`{{mu_county_mapped_2025_26}}`** county-mapped Irish students) originate from the commuter core of **Dublin (`{{cty_dublin_mu_2025_26}}`)**, **Kildare (`{{cty_kildare_mu_2025_26}}`**, where MU educates **`{{cty_kildare_mu_share_2025_26}}`** of all higher education students from the county), and **Meath (`{{cty_meath_mu_2025_26}}`**, **`{{cty_meath_mu_share_2025_26}}`** share), Maynooth draws **`{{mu_deprived_county_enrol_2025_26}}`** students (**`{{mu_deprived_county_share_2025_26}}`**, rated **`{{mu_rag_deprived_county}}`** against the **`{{rag_th_dep_green}}`** target) from the **`{{n_deprived_counties}}`** counties with below-average Pobal affluence (`score < 0`), substantially higher than Dublin university peers **DCU (`{{dcu_deprived_county_share_2025_26}}`)**, **UCD (`{{ucd_deprived_county_share_2025_26}}`)**, and **TCD (`{{tcd_deprived_county_share_2025_26}}`)**. This largely reflects Maynooth's location near the Midlands counties, not only institutional access activity. MU captures **`{{cty_longford_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_longford_mu_2025_26}}`**) of all HE students from **Co. Longford** (Pobal score **`{{cty_longford_rel_score}}`**), **`{{cty_westmeath_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_westmeath_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Westmeath** (**`{{cty_westmeath_rel_score}}`**), **`{{cty_cavan_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_cavan_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Cavan** (**`{{cty_cavan_rel_score}}`**), **`{{cty_offaly_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_offaly_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Offaly** (**`{{cty_offaly_rel_score}}`**), **`{{cty_leitrim_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_leitrim_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Leitrim** (**`{{cty_leitrim_rel_score}}`**), **`{{cty_laois_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_laois_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Laois** (**`{{cty_laois_rel_score}}`**), **`{{cty_wexford_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_wexford_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Wexford** (**`{{cty_wexford_rel_score}}`**), and **`{{cty_carlow_mu_share_2025_26}}`** (**`{{cty_carlow_mu_2025_26}}`**) from **Co. Carlow** (**`{{cty_carlow_rel_score}}`**).

