## Honest Analytical Boundaries & GDPR-Style Disclosure Control

Widening participation analytics requires strict separation between what public aggregate data can support and what requires restricted microdata. Detailed documentation is provided in [`docs/what_this_data_can_and_cannot_show.md`](docs/what_this_data_can_and_cannot_show.md):

1. **County-Level (Ecological) Deprivation, Not Individual-Level:** The Pobal HP 2022 link in Step 3 measures the socio-economic profile of a student's home county (`{{pobal_ed_count}}` Electoral Divisions aggregated by Census 2022 population weights to `{{n_counties}}` counties). Inferring that every student from a disadvantaged county is personally disadvantaged, or that students from affluent counties are personally affluent, is the **ecological fallacy**. Individual-level deprivation monitoring in Ireland uses the **HEA Deprivation Index Score (DIS)** linked to student home Eircodes/Small Areas inside institutional student records.
2. **No Disability or Ethnic Group Micro-Indicators in Public SRS Downloads:** Public HEA `Access our Data - Students` exports do not contain student disability status, DARE/HEAR indicator flags, QQI/FET basis of entry, or Irish Traveller / Roma identifiers. National Access Plan targets such as raising new entrants with disabilities to **`{{nap_disability_target}}`** are recorded in the KPI dictionary as requiring internal Access Office or HEA Equal Access Survey (EAS) returns.
3. **Nearest-`{{hea_rounding_base}}` Rounding and Small-Cell Suppression (`<{{small_cell_threshold}}`):** Published HEA SRS counts are independently rounded to the nearest **`{{hea_rounding_base}}`**. In addition, as a GDPR-style statistical disclosure control best practice, AccessLens-IE suppresses all non-zero cells below **`{{small_cell_threshold}}`** (i.e. published cells equal to `{{hea_rounding_base}}`) as `"<10"` in output display columns (`{{suppressed_inst_dim_cells}}` institution-dimension cells and `{{suppressed_county_inst_cells}}` county-institution cells, totalling **`{{suppressed_total_cells}}`** flagged small cells).
4. **HEA-Funded Institutional Scope:** The dataset covers the **`{{n_hea_institutions}}`** HEA-funded higher education institutions reporting to the SRS (`2019/2020` to `2025/2026`), noting that **National College of Ireland** entered SRS reporting scope in `2023/2024` (`{{dq_nci_pre_scope_years}}` structural zero years in `2019/2020` to `2022/2023` flagged in `gold.fact_institution_year`). Private/independent colleges outside HEA SRS are not included.
5. **Observational Patterns, No Causal Claims:** All correlations and comparisons reported in this repository are descriptive and observational.

